# Compile after HSL source changes

After any create, edit, or delete of files with extensions `.include`, `.hsl`, or `.hml` in this repository, run the compiler before finishing the task.

Use a single PowerShell session (activation does not persist across separate shells). Compile **this** folder against the subscribed Road to 56 workshop copy (read-only include base), not vanilla and not `_sandbox`:

```powershell
cd C:\Users\evgeny\Repos\HoI4\hsl
.\venv\Scripts\activate
python .\compiler.py "C:\Users\evgeny\Documents\Paradox Interactive\Hearts of Iron IV\mod\_sandbox-r56" "C:\Games\Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\394360\820260968"
```

- Do not skip this step after a batch of related source edits; one compile at the end of the batch is enough.
- If the compiler fails, fix the source and run the same commands again.
- Do not treat generated/output files as a substitute for compiling from `.include` / `.hsl` / `.hml`.
- The second path is read-only: never write, patch, or copy-into the workshop tree.
